---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

export { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
---

<Base
  title="MathsGuru"
  description="Free maths lessons for Sri Lankan students, Grade 6 to O-Level. Syllabus-matched, explained patiently, works on a phone."
>
  <div class="hero">
    <h1>Maths that makes sense</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Free maths lessons for Sri Lankan students, Grade 6 to O-Level. We follow
      the NIE syllabus exactly, explain every step, and tell you what went wrong
      when you get something wrong.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="promise">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">What you get here</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Every step explained.</strong> Not just what to do, but why that
        step works.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Real diagnoses.</strong> Get something wrong and we say exactly
        what went wrong and what to do instead. Never just "incorrect".
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Works on your phone.</strong> Low data, no downloads, no sign-up.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Free, and staying free.</strong> We will never charge a student
        for a lesson.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Start here</h2>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Grade 6 &mdash; Equivalent fractions</h3>
    <div class="card-meta">
      <span class="tag">NIE competency 3.2</span>
      <span class="tag">8 min lesson</span>
      <span class="tag">Term 2</span>
    </div>
    <p>
      Two different fractions can show exactly the same amount. This is the
      step that unlocks adding fractions, decimals, ratio and percentage, so it
      is worth getting right now.
    </p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button" href="/grade/6/3-2">Read the lesson</a>
      <a class="button button-quiet" href="/grade/6/3-2/practice">
        Go straight to practice
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Coming soon</h2>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Grade 6 &mdash; Adding and subtracting fractions</h3>
    <div class="card-meta">
      <span class="tag">NIE competency 3.4</span>
      <span class="tag">Planned</span>
    </div>
    <p>Once equivalent fractions is solid, this is the natural next step.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Grade 6 &mdash; Ratio and rate</h3>
    <div class="card-meta">
      <span class="tag">NIE competency 4.1</span>
      <span class="tag">Planned</span>
    </div>
    <p>Everyday uses: discounts, speeds, mixing, sharing things out fairly.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
